@startuml 06-keys-and-envelope
title Protocol 06 - Key hierarchy and block encryption

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle
hide empty members

class "Account key (AK)" as ak <<secret>> {
  256-bit random, created on the first device
  stored in the platform SecureStore
  backed up as a 24-word recovery phrase
  reaches other devices only via pairing
}

class "Note key" as nk <<derived>> {
  {field} HKDF-SHA256(AK, info = "notes/v1/note" | note_id)
  one per note, recomputed on demand
}

class "Recovery verifier" as rv <<derived>> {
  {field} HKDF-SHA256(AK, info = "notes/v1/recovery")
  server stores SHA-256 of it
}

class "Blob key" as bk <<secret>> {
  256-bit random, one per attachment
  stored inside the attachment block payload
}

class "Pairing key (K)" as pk <<ephemeral>> {
  SPAKE2 output, lives for one pairing
  wraps { account_id, AK } for the new device
}

class "Device token" as tok <<secret>> {
  256-bit random, issued by the server
  authenticates the device, encrypts nothing
  server stores SHA-256 of it
}

class "BlockPayload (plaintext)" as payload {
  schema : 1
  kind : header | paragraph | heading | todo | code | attachment
  order : fractional index string
  text : string
  attrs : map
}

class "BlockEnvelope (on the wire and on the server)" as env {
  block_id : uuid
  note_id : uuid
  version : hybrid logical clock string
  deleted : bool
  nonce : 12 random bytes
  {field} ciphertext : AES-256-GCM(note key, nonce, payload, AAD)
}

class "AAD (authenticated, not encrypted)" as aad {
  "notes/v1" | block_id | note_id | version | deleted
}

ak --> nk : derives
ak --> rv : derives
nk --> env : encrypts
payload --> env : becomes ciphertext
aad --> env : bound into the tag
payload --> bk : attachment block carries
pk ..> ak : transports once

note right of aad
  Because ids, version and the deleted flag are bound
  into the authentication tag, the server cannot
  move a ciphertext to another block or note,
  replay it under a different version,
  or turn a block into a tombstone or back.
end note

note bottom of env
  version format, 24 characters, compared bytewise:
  12 hex digits unix time in ms
  4 hex digits counter
  8 hex digits device tag
  A tombstone has deleted = true and an empty payload.
end note

note bottom of nk
  Random 96-bit nonces are safe here because each key
  only encrypts the blocks of one note.
end note

@enduml
